The 2026 manager presentation lists the measures followed for the fund:

- **Global exposure**, with the commitment approach, against the 100% limit;
- **Concentration** by issuer (the 5/10/40 rule included), country and sector;
- **Liquidity**: the share of the portfolio that can be sold within one, five and twenty days;
- **Ex-ante tracking error** against the index, for information, with an indicative range of 3% to 8% (5.1% at 30 June 2026);
- **Stress tests**, run each month on historical and hypothetical scenarios;
- **Counterparty exposure** on the currency forwards of the hedged share class.

Hard limits are coded in the order management system and block a trade before it is placed; the risk team checks every limit again each day, after the trades.

When a limit is breached, the procedure in the presentation is: the risk team informs the portfolio managers and compliance the same day; an active breach is corrected at once, and any loss is paid back to the fund by the management company; a passive breach is corrected in the best interest of investors, normally within five business days. Every breach is entered in a breach register and reported to the conducting officers, to the board at its next meeting and to the depositary, and, when material, to the Luxembourg regulator.

The 2025 prospectus and the 2025 annual report name the same three firms:

- **Depositary**: Example Depositary Bank S.A., Luxembourg;
- **Administrator** (central administration, registrar and transfer agent): Example Fund Administration S.A., Luxembourg;
- **Auditor**: Example Audit S.à r.l., Luxembourg, approved statutory auditor, which signed an unqualified audit report on the 2025 accounts.

The **ongoing charges** at 31 December 2025 are **1.74% for the A USD Acc class**, according to its key information document, and **1.07% for the I USD Acc class**, according to the 2025 annual report. They include the management fee and the fund's operating costs, but neither the performance fee nor the transaction costs. The documents provided give no figure for the A EUR Hedged Acc and I EUR Dist classes.

The statement of expenses in the 2025 annual report gives the main items paid by the fund in 2025:

- management fees: USD 4.32 million;
- performance fees (I classes): USD 0.41 million;
- central administration: USD 0.26 million;
- depositary and custody: USD 0.21 million;
- professional fees, audit and other costs: USD 0.17 million;
- Luxembourg subscription tax: USD 0.14 million.

Transaction costs, mainly brokerage commissions, came to USD 0.58 million in 2025. **Research** is paid by the management company out of its own resources, not by the fund (2025 prospectus).
